COMMERCIAL SOFTWARE LICENCE — chatbot (Suvida Chatbot derivative)
Intelligent Waste Collection Network · HACQUIRE 2026

1. ORIGIN AND CHAIN OF TITLE

   This module derives from the Suvida Chatbot, acquired from
   AniketCodes76/suvida_chatbot at commit e207819. The acquisition covered
   the FastAPI service shell, the /chat request/response contract, and the
   local-LLM integration pattern.

   Any onward transfer must disclose that chain of title. A buyer acquires
   this derivative work and whatever rights the seller holds in the
   underlying acquisition — no more. Verify the upstream licence terms
   independently before relying on them.

2. GRANT

   Perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive licence to use, modify, host and
   sublicense this module and its accompanying files, including for
   commercial purposes.

3. TRANSFERABILITY

   This licence is assignable in whole to a successor in interest, once,
   on written notice. Nothing in this module depends on any other module
   in the registry: dependencies are reached over HTTP at URLs supplied by
   environment variable, and every one of them degrades. Transfer requires
   no code change on either side.

4. WHAT IS AND IS NOT INCLUDED

   INCLUDED
     · chatbot.py — the whole module: datastore, adapters, HTTP surface
     · mocks/vendor_prompt_transport.txt — the original TravelBuddy
       public-transport persona, preserved verbatim from the acquisition.
       It has standalone value to a transit operator and is conveyed with
       this licence.
     · mocks/conversations.json — sample audit records

   NOT INCLUDED
     · Any language model, model weights, or Ollama installation. The LLM
       is optional; with OLLAMA_URL unset the module is fully functional
       using deterministic intent routing and templated replies.
     · The other six modules of the network, or any right to them.
     · Operational data. No datastore, uploads directory or .env file
       forms part of a transfer.

5. DISCLOSED DEFECT, REMEDIED

   The acquired code authenticated with `x_api_key != os.getenv("API_KEY")`
   and no fallback. With the variable unset — the state of any fresh
   clone — both sides evaluated to None and unauthenticated callers were
   admitted. This build fails closed. A buyer inheriting any other fork of
   the upstream project should assume the defect is present in it.

6. CREDENTIALS

   The default key `dev-suvida-key` is public knowledge: it is the
   fallback compiled into the source so a fresh clone runs. It is a
   development convenience and not a security control. Change CHAT_API_KEY
   before exposing this service beyond localhost.

7. WARRANTY

   Provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The seller warrants
   only that it has the right to grant this licence.
